      "content": "I'm not a doctor, but I can suggest that you see a doctor to get a proper diagnosis. Taking a large amount of ibuprofen every few hours may not be the best approach, as it could increase the risk of stomach damage and other side effects. It's also possible that the pain is related to a more serious injury, such as a herniated disc or strain on internal organs, rather than just a pulled muscle. Would you consider scheduling an urgent care visit or consulting your primary care physician instead?",
